WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.302
- Oh, he just wanted to
give us some time alone.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:05.972
NARRATOR: Anne Heche first
rose to Fame on the soap opera,

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.174
"Another World",
playing the dual roles

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:13.146
of twins, Vicky Hudson and
Marley Love from 1987 to 1991.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.181
It earned her a
Daytime Emmy award

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:18.351
and led to films like "Donnie
Brasco", "Six Days, Seven

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.952
Nights", and "Wag the Dog".

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:23.122
But it was her highly
publicized romantic relationship

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.992
with Ellen DeGeneres in
the late 90s that really

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.126
put her in the spotlight.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.962
- Ellen is to me the embodiment
of both male and female.

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:33.666
I think that's why our energies
connected so quickly and so

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:38.204
easily, because I've
always felt in my being

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:39.705
that I'm both male and female.

00:00:39.738 --> 00:00:41.808
NARRATOR: They were
considered one of Hollywood's

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.377
first lesbian power
couples before breaking

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.646
up after 3 and 1/2 years.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.382
Heche said that she believed
it damaged her career

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.217
and cost her roles.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.418
- This is impossible.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.587
NARRATOR: Heche eventually
bounced back though,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.823
in both her career
and personal life.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.891
She appeared in
numerous TV shows

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.461
and was married for eight
years to Coleman Laffoon.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.595
They had a son.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.997
She also shared a son with
her former "Men in Trees"

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.199
co-star, James Tupper.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.634 line:0%
- Even though I was
in therapy for years,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.537 line:0%
I never told anybody that
I had another personality,

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.507 line:0%
I never told anybody that I
heard voices and spoke to God,

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.142 line:0%
I never told anybody any of it.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.177 line:0%
NARRATOR: The actress was
open about her battles

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.378 line:0%
with mental illness.

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:21.948 line:0%
In her 2001 memoir,
"Call Me Crazy",

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.984 line:0%
she wrote about enduring
sexual abuse as a child.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:28.187
Heche was hospitalized
in 2000 after wandering

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.190
in rural California knocking
on a stranger's door

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.558
and making strange statements.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:36.262 line:0%
- I think I was at the
bitter, bitter end.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.598 line:0%
I was in a place where
I was ready to leave

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.867 line:0%
this planet on my spaceship.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.604
NARRATOR: A fiery 2022 car
crash put her in a coma

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.906
and left her with severe burns.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.742
Anne Heche led a life of
public highs and lows.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.978
But through it all,
she shined on screen

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.346
and strived to stay hopeful.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.548
- I've always wanted
to heal my life,

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.151
I've always wanted to see
the good side of life,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.886
I've always wanted to see
the good in everything

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.954
that happened to me.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:04.157
And I could not be happier
with who I am right now.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.092 line:0%
I couldn't be happier
with what I've been

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.727 line:0%
able to accomplish in my life.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.497
[MUSIC PLAYING]

